# Monorepo Structure

This project is a monorepo managed by pnpm and nx/lerna.

The root of the monorepo is src folder (which is not the git root). The builds folder contains the builds for the different platforms.
Currently, only the darwin build is supported, but in future Windows will be supported as well.
The code in the @trici/desktop package is built for prod (js bundle and swift console apps) and then copied to the builds/darwin folder.


The docs folder contains the documentation for the project.
.
├── builds
│   └── darwin
├── docs
├── src
│   ├── node_modules
│   ├── packages
│   └── scripts
└── venv
    ├── bin
    ├── include
    └── lib



Each package has its own tests which is located in the __tests__ folder. For example:

├── packages
│   ├── activmon
│   │   ├── __tests__
│   │   ├── dist
│   │   └── src
│   ├── app-observer
│   │   ├── __tests__
│   │   ├── bin
│   │   │   └── dev
│   │   ├── dist
│   │   ├── logs
│   │   └── src
│   │       └── swift


There are basically two types of packages: oine which contain native code and ones which just have js code. The ones with the native code will have a native folder like src/swift for swift code. 

## Building of packages
The package.json of each package has a "build-dev" and "build-prod" command which is used to build the package. There is no "build" command. The "build-dev" and "build-prod" commands typically use esbuild to build the typescript code and if there is native code then there is a separate added step for that. E.g. 

 "scripts": {
    "esbuild-dev": "cross-env NODE_ENV=development node esbuild.js ",
    "esbuild-prod": "cross-env NODE_ENV=production node esbuild.js ",
    "build-types": "tsc && node ../../scripts/flatten-types.js .",
    "build-dev": "run-script-os",
    "build-dev:darwin": "pnpm run buildBinary-dev:darwin && pnpm run esbuild-dev && pnpm run build-types",
    "build-dev:win32": "pnpm run buildBinary-dev:win32 && pnpm run esbuild-dev && pnpm run build-types",
    "buildBinary-dev:darwin": "if [ -f 'bin/dev/Recorder' ]; then rm -rf bin/dev/Recorder; fi && xcodebuild -project src/swift/Recorder/Recorder.xcodeproj -scheme Recorder -configuration Debug -derivedDataPath src/swift/Recorder/build && cp src/swift/Recorder/build/Build/Products/Debug/Recorder bin/dev/Recorder && shasum -a 256 bin/dev/Recorder > dist/Recorder.sha256",
    "buildBinary-prod:darwin": "if [ -f 'bin/Recorder' ]; then rm -rf bin/Recorder; fi && xcodebuild -project src/swift/Recorder/Recorder.xcodeproj -scheme Recorder -configuration Release -derivedDataPath src/swift/Recorder/build && cp src/swift/Recorder/build/Build/Products/Release/Recorder bin/Recorder && shasum -a 256 bin/Recorder > dist/Recorder.sha256",
    "build-prod": "run-script-os",
    "build-prod:darwin": "pnpm run buildBinary-prod:darwin && pnpm run esbuild-prod && pnpm run build-types",
    "build-prod:win32": "pnpm run buildBinary-prod:win32 && pnpm run esbuild-prod && pnpm run build-types",
    "test": "node ./__tests__/recorder.test.js"
  },

  In the above example, you can see that the build-dev is calling build-Binary-dev:darwin to build the native swift code and the esbuild-dev to build the typescript code and the build-types to run typescript to just output the types. 

  Each package thus will also necessarily have an esbuild.js file and a tsconfig.json for esbuild and typescript respectively. The tsconfig.json file inherits from the tsconfig.json at the root of the monorepo. 

  In packages where the tests are generated using jest, a jest.config.js file is also present at the root of the package. 

 ## Models/Entitites

 The data structures/models/entitites/types that are used across the application are typically defined in the @trici/models package. If any new models are to be added or modified it should be done in that package. The @trici/models package is referenced by other packages. 


